                "textDirection": "ltr",
                "fontVariantId": "normal-400",
                "textDecoration": "none",
                "letterSpacing": "0",
                "fills": [
                  {
                    "fillColor": "#a3adbd",
                    "fillOpacity": 1
                  }
                ],
                "fontFamily": "Arimo",
                "text": "A hold that clears (Track Hold = Clear track, or a Custom pedal whose Hold is Clear or Clear all) fills the held pedal's LED pill: red grows from both ends toward the centre over the long-press time (800 ms by default). The track clears when the ends meet; once the clear is accepted the board confirms it by flashing the full red pill 3 times, 120 ms on and 120 ms off (about 0.7 s), on its own clock, and the pill shows the empty-track state. The flash is not cut short by the app's next pill frame or the stale-fill time; a new hold on that pill takes over, and each pill flashes on its own clock. On a pill already red (a recording track, or any red state) the pill's own red drops to about a third while the hold runs and the fill is drawn at full brightness; releasing early restores it at once. Releasing early, a mode change, a lost link, or a hold that can no longer fire ends the fill at once. With two clear holds pending the newest fills, and the older one fills again if the newer settles first. Wire: optional CLEAR_HOLD message (progress every 20 ms, 255 once when it fires), console firmware 2.6, protocol 12. No screen mirrors the LED pill. Note: with default colours a held track pedal reads white (pressed), so the dimmed-red case shows where the pill's shown colour is red."
              }
            ],
            "textTransform": "none",
            "textAlign": "left",
            "fontId": "custom-99a2c890-1804-450c-8af8-6b60ee9a6b27",
            "fontSize": "24",
            "fontWeight": "400",
